@startuml analyse-parcours-p3
title Web journey analysis workflow — Page 3/5 : Core Web Vitals + HTML report

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam participant {
  BackgroundColor #E0F0F4
  BorderColor #5BA1BC
  FontColor #1C2856
}
skinparam actor {
  BackgroundColor #E0F0F4
  BorderColor #5BA1BC
  FontColor #1C2856
}
skinparam ArrowColor #5BA1BC
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #5BA1BC
skinparam SequenceGroupBodyBackgroundColor #ECECF2
skinparam SequenceGroupBorderColor #5BA1BC
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #E0F0F4
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9BD0DD
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 200
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor "User" as U #82C1DD
participant "Claude\n(skill analyse-parcours)" as C #82C1DD
participant "collect_cwv_pagespeed.py" as CW #C8E6C9
participant "run_lighthouse.sh" as LH #C8E6C9
participant "generate_report_html.py" as GR #DBDDE5
database "audit-dir/" as FS #9BD0DD

== Step 37 — Core Web Vitals ==

alt cwv.json already present
  C -> C : [Step 37] cwv.json present - CWV collection skipped
else GOOGLE_API_KEY available (priority path)
  C -> CW : python3 collect_cwv_pagespeed.py <audit-dir>
  CW -> CW : PageSpeed Insights API\n(CrUX field + Lighthouse lab, per page)
  CW -> FS : cwv.json {lcp, inp, cls, source: "pagespeed/crux"}
  FS -> C : cwv.json generated
else GOOGLE_API_KEY absent (fallback)
  C -> LH : bash run_lighthouse.sh <audit-dir>
  LH -> FS : Extract URLs from .har\n(log.pages[].title, deduplicated)
  LH -> LH : npx lighthouse <url> per page\n(lab mode, network simulation)
  LH -> FS : cwv.json {lcp, inp, cls per page}
  FS -> C : cwv.json generated
  note over LH
    If Lighthouse unavailable:
    warning + report without CWV (HAR onLoad used as LCP proxy).
    Relaunch: "rerun Lighthouse".
  end note
end

== Step 40 — HTML report ==

C -> GR : python3 generate_report_html.py <audit-dir>
GR -> FS : Read .har
FS -> GR : Raw network traffic
GR -> FS : Read coverage-analysis.json
FS -> GR : Dead JS/CSS code metrics
GR -> FS : Read cwv.json (if present)
FS -> GR : LCP / INP / CLS per page
GR -> FS : Read efootprint-python-summary.json (if present)
FS -> GR : CO2e totals + hypotheses
GR -> FS : Read eof-audit-results.json + eof-radar-<domain>.svg (if present)
FS -> GR : EOF answers (measured + questionnaire merged\nby merge_lots.py) + 6-dimension radar

note over GR, FS
  Report sections (in order):
  1. Header: date, domains, page count, source files
  2. Prioritized recommendations (P1 red / P2 orange / P3 green)
  3. GreenIT best practices
  4. Core Web Vitals (if cwv.json - LCP/INP/CLS with Google thresholds)
  5. CO2e environmental impact (if efootprint-python-summary.json - skill /efootprint)
  6. EOF optimization potential (if eof-audit-results.json - 6-dimension radar,
     "measured" answers + questionnaire merged by merge_lots.py)
  7. Appendices: EcoIndex dashboard, Network traffic, Dead code, detailed CWV
  If cwv.json absent: LCP shows HAR onLoad with an explicit note.
  CO2e section omitted if efootprint-python-summary.json absent.
  EOF section omitted if eof-audit-results.json absent (run_eof.py not run yet).
end note

GR -> GR : check_report_values.py (internal, non-blocking)\ndetects badly substituted values (None%, NaN, {{...}})
GR -> C : journey-report-YYYY-MM-DD.html
C -> U : Report delivered:\n<audit-dir>/journey-report-YYYY-MM-DD.html

@enduml
